WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.840
Every Friday in Jerusalem, Franciscan
friars lead a procession through narrow

2
00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.340
old streets.

3
00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:10.000
Pilgrims stop to pray at
14 Stations of the Cross,

4
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.010
along a route called the Way of Sorrows.

5
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:16.360
Some have travelled thousands
of miles to be here.

6
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.850
Yet many Christians believe
God can be worshipped anywhere.

7
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.000
So why travel so far to
pray, if God is everywhere?

8
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.260
In this mission, you'll walk
through Jerusalem on a map,

9
00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:29.940
from Gethsemane to the Holy Sepulchre.

10
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:35.880
Then you'll see why Catholics, Orthodox and
Protestants rate pilgrimage so differently.

11
00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.200
Your mission: find out why
Christians travel so far to pray.
